   "source": [
    "# Sigma‑Hole Docking Pipeline – Google Colab\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook lets you run the sigma‑hole docking pipeline from a GitHub repository.\n",
    "It will:\n",
    "1️⃣ Clone your repository (set `REPO_URL` below)\n",
    "2️⃣ Install required packages\n",
    "3️⃣ List available files\n",
    "4️⃣ Let you upload any additional data (ligand structures, receptor, MO surface‑analysis files, or a ready‑made CSV)\n",
    "5️⃣ Extract Vmax values from `*_surfanalysis.txt` files\n",
    "6️⃣ Build an input CSV (compound_id, smiles, halogen, vmax) – automatically from SDF files if available\n",
    "7️⃣ Select a receptor\n",
    "8️⃣ Run the sigma‑hole pipeline\n",
    "9️⃣ Visualise and save results\n",
    "\n",
    "**Tip:** Keep your private data (e.g., the `MO` folder) local and upload them via the file‑upload widget – they are **not** committed to the repo."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "## @title 1. Configuration\n",
    "REPO_URL = \"https://github.com/Hich00b/sigma-hole-docking-project\"  # @param {type:\"string\"}\n",
    "REPO_DIR = \"sigma-hole-docking-colab\"  # @param {type:\"string\"}\n",
    "print(f\"\"\"Repository: {REPO_URL}\nClone dir:  {REPO_DIR}\n\"\"\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
